Prompt 1: Understand the starter code (after you deploy it)
Read-only on the org: do not deploy, create, or modify anything there, and do not run sf agent preview or sf agent test. You may only write files under .inventory/.

1. Read the README, any docs, and sfdx-project.json. List what the project contains: custom objects and fields, flows (name, type, active or not), Apex classes (flag @InvocableMethod), agent bundles (aiAuthoringBundles), prompt templates, and any seed data.
2. Run only these org queries:
- sf data query -q "SELECT LanguageLocaleKey FROM Organization"
- sf data query -q "SELECT MasterLabel FROM PermissionSetLicense WHERE Status='Active'"
- sf data query -q "SELECT DeveloperName, MasterLabel FROM BotDefinition"
- sf data query -q "SELECT ApiName, ProcessType FROM FlowDefinitionView WHERE IsActive = true"
- SELECT COUNT() for each custom object found (max 5)
3. Save the results as text files in .inventory/.

Output only, under 40 lines:
A) Is there an agent already? (none / partial in project / already in org) + its API name
B) What the starter gives me: objects, flows, Apex actions, agent subagents/actions
C) Red flags: empty objects, inactive flows, TODOs, hints in the README
Prompt 2: Plan and build (after the challenge is revealed)
CHALLENGE (summary):
{{3–6 lines in your own words: who the users are, what they need to do, which data, constraints}}

Use .inventory/* and the existing project. Read the agentforce-generate skill references to confirm syntax. Do not write any files until I approve.

1. Split the challenge into max 5 requirements (core user journey only).
2. Table: Requirement | What already covers it (subagent / action / flow / Apex) | DONE / MODIFY / NEW | What to change
3. Plan per subagent: Action | KEEP / MODIFY / NEW | Source | Inputs | Returns

Rules:
- If an agent exists, extend it and keep all existing API names. If none exists, create one named {{Agent_Api_Name}}.
- Reuse starter flows, Apex and standard actions before creating new ones.
- No new objects or fields unless unavoidable; flag them instead.
- Users speak French: all user-facing text in French, API names in English (ASCII), never translate picklist values.
