STOP and wait for my approval.

After I approve: edit only what's marked MODIFY or NEW, run sf agent validate authoring-bundle, then deploy only the changed components (flows, then AiAuthoringBundle). If anything fails, stop and show me the exact error with a proposed fix. Do NOT publish or activate.
Prompt 3: Smoke test
Smoke-test the deployed bundle {{Agent_Api_Name}} with live actions:
sf agent preview start --json --use-live-actions --authoring-bundle {{Agent_Api_Name}}
then sf agent preview send for each utterance, then sf agent preview end.
(If a flag is rejected, check --help and adapt.)

First run one sf data query --json "SELECT ... LIMIT 20" to get real record values. Never invent names. If no records come back, stop and tell me.

Max 8 utterances, in French, as real users write:
- one per action (formal)
- one informal or with a typo
- one with no results, one with multiple matches
- one off-topic: "Quel temps fait-il à Paris ?"
- one in English, to check the agent still replies in French

Pass = right subagent, right action, reply in French, fixed texts match exactly.
Output only: table # | utterance | subagent | action | French? | PASS/FAIL | cause. Then one proposed fix per FAIL. Don't change files yet.
Prompt 4: Fix and re-test
Apply the fixes you proposed. Deploy only what changed, validate the bundle, then re-run the full smoke test list in a new preview session. Output the same table, with changed rows marked.
(Repeat until everything passes, or you’re happy with it.)
Prompt 5: Publish and activate
Show me what you're about to publish and wait for my OK. Then:
sf agent publish authoring-bundle --json --api-name {{Agent_Api_Name}}
sf agent activate --json --api-name {{Agent_Api_Name}}
Then verify with 3 utterances from the smoke test (one per main action + off-topic):
sf agent preview start --json --api-name {{Agent_Api_Name}}
If publish fails, stop and show the exact error.
Output: publish status, activate status, 3-row results table.
Prompt 6 (optional, if you have time): Formal test suite
Create a test spec for {{Agent_Api_Name}} at specs/{{Agent_Api_Name}}-testSpec.yaml (confirm the YAML keys in the skill references). 10–12 cases: every action, no-result, multiple-match, off-topic, one English input. Utterances and expected outcomes in French; subagent and action names exactly as in the bundle.
Show me the spec first. After I approve, create and run it:
sf agent test create --json --spec specs/{{Agent_Api_Name}}-testSpec.yaml --api-name {{Agent_Api_Name}}_Tests
sf agent test run --json --api-name {{Agent_Api_Name}}_Tests --wait 10
Output only: pass rate, and a table of failures with the cause.
